00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
frustrating fart jokes workplace  frenemies and full-on egomania the nutty  professor might be hilarious but behind  the scenes the film was far from a  laughing matter  jerry lewis movies were popular with  kids and he always strove to make  entertainment the entire family could  enjoy while the nutty professor was of  course popular with young tykes it was  surprisingly geared more towards an  adult audience paramount was concerned  about the nutty professor because it was  more of an adult film or as adult as  jerry lewis could get as it turned out  the film was a big crowd-pleasing hit  for people of all ages while earning  jerry lewis some of the best reviews of  his career it would also be lewis's peak  as a filmmaker the ultimate culmination  of his skills as a funny man and writer  director in 2004 the nutty professor was  entered into the library of congress as  an important comedy that will be  preserved for generations to come  when eddie murphy wanted to remake the  nutty professor he had to go to jerry  lewis directly because he owned the  rights the film was going to feature a  louis cameo before he decided to back  out the reason too many fart jokes lewis  confirmed to entertainment weekly when  he had to do fart jokes he lost me  who they called my name yeah i called  you up your name it  even though the nutty professor remake  turned out well with decent reviews and  strong box office lewis eventually  regretted letting the picture move  forward lewis told entertainment weekly  i have such respect for eddie but i  shouldn't have done it what i did was  perfect the first time around and all  you're going to do is diminish that  perfection by letting someone else do it  like many comedians eddie murphy used  saturday night live as the launching pad  for his success after the box office  success of 48 hours murphy's career took  off like a rocket the actor would soon  make a trio of hits with trading places  beverly hills copping coming to america  after he made coming to america however  murphy's career took a nosedive with  bombs like harlem knights boomerang and  the painfully unfunny beverly hills cop  three murphy desperately needed a hit  and the nutty professor felt like it was  make or break thankfully eddie murphy  pulled it off and the nutty professor  was indeed a big success making 273  million worldwide it also got mostly  positive notices from critics who were  delighted that murphy was finally funny  again  not only was the nutty professor a big  hit when eddie murphy needed it it was  also the beginning of a new phase of his  career where he was doing more  family-friendly entertainment back in  the 80s murphy was known for his  outrageous down and dirty brand of  comedy in order to reinvent himself he  had to play a more vulnerable role and  leave his usual slick wisecracking foul  mouse persona behind him brian grazer  who produced the nutty professor told  the la times the only way to do that is  have him play a character that is  vulnerable it strips away eddie's  coolness for a while and is a role that  allows him not to be in control or  powerful in the beginning after the  nutty professor murphy had some of the  biggest hits of his career with more  family-friendly films like dr doolittle  daddy daycare and of course the animated  blockbuster shrek you must bleach or  something cause that is one dazzling  smile you got there and do i detect a  hint of minty freshness  he was also nominated for an oscar for  his performance in dream girls proving  he had even greater range and depth than  many people realized  in 1978 john landis established himself  as an a-list director when he helmed  national lampoon's animal house which  was the biggest comedy hit of its time  i'm a zit  get it  landis also directed eddie murphy in the  smash hits trading places and coming to  america but landis and murphy had a  difficult working relationship on coming  to america landis revealed to collider  the guy on trading places was young and  full of energy and curious and funny and  fresh and great the guy on coming to  america was the pig of the world  eventually landis and murphy patched  things up and worked together again on  beverly hills cop3 it was also revealed  that landis nearly directed the nutty  professor according to a report in the  los angeles times landis was eager to  come aboard it's not clear why he didn't  helm the movie but landis and murphy  reportedly remain cordial with landis  telling empire i see eddie around  occasionally i drive by we wave  while another landis murphy pairing  didn't come together tom shadiak who  just had a big hit with ace ventura pet  detective came aboard instead amounting  to a big step up in his directing career  in fact after the success of the nutty  professor shadyac became a comedy  powerhouse directing jim carrey again  and liar liar and bruce almighty over  time however shadyac had a spiritual  awakening after suffering a bicycling  accident in 2007 that left him with some  lingering brain issues as he recovered  he decided to sell his mansion and live  in a trailer park in malibu he also gave  away a substantial amount of money  telling cbs the more i give away the  wealthier i feel shadyac's spiritual  journey was chronicled in the  documentary i am and as he said in  pepperdine university's online magazine  the accident didn't create a wisdom  moment i simply got knocked from my head  to my heart and had the courage to talk  about the hypocrisy i'd woken up to in  my life  in both versions of the nutty professor  buddy love is an egotistical jerk some  feel the character isn't too far from  jerry lewis and eddie murphy in real  life  you rude discourteous egomaniac you're  crazy about me right and i can  understand it as landis revealed in an  interview with collider murphy reached a  point where he really got carried away  with himself murphy even admitted to the  seattle times i've had periods when i  wasn't grounded anytime you saw me in a  leather suit with a leather glove with a  ring on the outside of the glove at that  period i'm not grounded jerry lewis  wasn't exactly mr humble either as  critic jonathan rosenbaum observed in  american movie classics magazine part of  what's so disturbing about buddy love is  that lewis clearly knows him like the  back of his hand film historian jay  niber also noted in the new york post  everybody's got a jekyll and hyde  personality and buddy was jerry lewis's  mr hyde  one of eddie murphy's most important  creative partners is legendary makeup  artist rick baker who provided  pioneering effects for an american  werewolf in london thriller and men in  black to name a few baker and murphy  worked together on a number of films and  their partnership on the nutty professor  was probably their most groundbreaking  collaboration baker did the makeup for  coming to america which is the first  time murphy hilariously played multiple  characters with the nutty professor  murphy took the multiple character idea  even further playing a total of seven  people including sherman's mother and  father who make hilarious banter around  the dinner table the nutty professor was  one of baker's most challenging makeup  jobs yet he told the new york post eddie  was so polite and cooperative he  actually enjoys the process of becoming  someone else eddie would disappear so  completely as soon as i slipped that  mask over his face  when the nutty professor came out there  was no such term as fat shaming and fat  people had long been an easy target of  cruel jokes yet from the beginning  murphy wanted to show a more  compassionate look at being heavyset  before the nutty professor shoot murphy  told the los angeles times america is  obsessed with weight you have to look a  certain way there will be fat jokes at  every turn but this movie is not a put  down of fat people with at least one  plus size performer the nutty professor  hit a nerve hop singer lizzo recently  told variety that she related in an  emotional way to a scene in which  professor clump opens a drawer to reveal  a secret stash of candy lizzo told the  outlet i could literally cry right now  thinking about it people around me were  laughing but i hide food too i feel them  i feel sympathy and empathy for him  jada pinkett smith played sherman  clump's love interest carla purdy in the  nutty professor the role was a big step  up for pinkett smith's career except  that she hated the wig she was forced to  wear as she recalled on red table talk  they put me in some crazy wigs for sure  where people didn't really know enough  about black hair to know how to make  wigs and what wigs should look like  smith called the wig she had to wear a  rough one adding that the woman who  created it did not have a good grasp of  how black women wore and styled their  own hair after that pinkett smith had  her own hairdresser on every subsequent  film  while the second nutty professor film  nutty professor 2 the clumps wasn't the  box office powerhouse that the first  movie was the sequel still did well so  it's not surprising that there's been  another remake in the works but the real  surprise is who's planning the new  version james vanderbilt who wrote the  david fincher true crime classic zodiac  as well as scream 5 managed to secure  the rights for a nutty professor remake  it's strange to think that the  screenwriter behind such scary and grim  entertainment could be spearheading the  next nutty professor film and it  definitely feels like an odd fit but  maybe vanderbilt can come up with a  whole new imaginative spin on the story  for today's audiences ultimately the  nutty professor movies have a terrific  legacy the original will always be  considered jerry lewis's best known work  and eddie murphy was able to create a  surprisingly empathetic update that made  audiences howl with laughter if there  are more nutty professor movies in the  future here's hoping they can deliver  the same good message of self-love and  individuality that worked so well before  [Music]

